          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Kent L. Richland (Petitioner), according to Kent L. Richland (Petitioner), the case concerns whether a federal bankruptcy court can exercise jurisdiction over a tort claim that is the primary source of payment to creditors, given the Ninth Circuit\u2019s broad interpretation of the probate exception."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner and Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f7654adc7345c2cc6912d9ccd1a0bb876231e41fa8eee51a362ee855d7fc4323",
